From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:59:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: Do not advertise a hot-plug slot without a
 hot-plug driver

The Qualcomm Root Ports keep the hardware's Hot-Plug Capable bit in Slot
Capabilities; qcom_pcie_set_slot_cap() only sets NCCS and clears ABP.
When the kernel is built without the PCIe hotplug driver,
pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses D3 for such a port, because
pciehp_is_native() returns false whenever CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE is
off, and the port driver leaves runtime PM off for it. The port then
stays in D0 through system suspend, pci_host_common_d3cold_possible()
fails, and the controller keeps the link up together with its clocks
and its minimum interconnect vote.

On the OnePlus Pad 4 (SM8850, WCN7860 Wi-Fi on PCIe 0) this kept a DDR
and NoC vote in the RPMh sleep set and the PCIe clocks prepared in
s2idle, with or without the Wi-Fi driver bound: the SoC never reached
DDR low power or CX collapse.

Clear Hot-Plug Capable when CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE is not enabled.
Nothing in such a kernel services the slot, so the bit only blocks D3
and reserves bus and memory padding behind the port. Kernels with the
hotplug driver keep the slot as it is.

With the change, over four s2idle cycles on the Pad 4: the Root Port and
the Wi-Fi endpoint suspend to D3hot every time, the controller turns the
link off and releases its clocks, the RPMh sleep set holds no bus vote,
and the SoC enters DDR low power and CX collapse in every sleep. The
Wi-Fi is back after each resume. The endpoint does not acknowledge
PME_Turn_Off in time ("Timeout waiting for L2 entry"); the DWC core
treats that as non-fatal and the link comes back normally.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index 9d755a3a780f..0e36ac4e3f4a 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -396,6 +396,14 @@ static void qcom_pcie_set_slot_cap(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	 * Attention Button Present in Slot Capabilities.
 	 */
 	val &= ~PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_ABP;
+
+	/*
+	 * Without the PCIe hotplug driver nobody services the slot, and the
+	 * PCI core never lets a hot-plug capable port go to D3: the link
+	 * would then stay up through system suspend.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE))
+		val &= ~PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPC;
 	writel(val, pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
 
 	dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_dis(pci);
-- 
